# A reserved word as a column name: DS0126 with a fix that quotes it.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | extend null = 1, true = 2
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..46
  PIPELINE@0..45
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    EXTEND_OP@20..45
      IDENT@20..26 "extend"
      WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@27..35
        NAME@27..31
          NULL_KW@27..31 "null"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        EQ@32..33 "="
        WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
        LITERAL@34..35
          LONG@34..35 "1"
      COMMA@35..36 ","
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@37..45
        NAME@37..41
          TRUE_KW@37..41 "true"
        WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
        EQ@42..43 "="
        WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
        LITERAL@44..45
          LONG@44..45 "2"
  WHITESPACE@45..46 "\n"

error[DS0126]: `null` is a reserved word
  --> query:1:28
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | extend null = 1, true = 2
  |                            ^^^^ a reserved word cannot be a name without quotes
  |
  = help: to use it as a name, quote it: `['null']`

error[DS0126]: `true` is a reserved word
  --> query:1:38
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | extend null = 1, true = 2
  |                                      ^^^^ a reserved word cannot be a name without quotes
  |
  = help: to use it as a name, quote it: `['true']`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | extend ['null'] = 1, ['true'] = 2
which parses without errors
